    "abstract": null,
    "field": "Antarctic climate and surface mass balance",
    "problem": "Large uncertainties in estimating Antarctica's surface mass balance persist because climate models struggle to accurately represent complex polar processes like drifting snow and cloud physics amid scarce observational data and high natural climate variability.",
    "method": "The paper proposes improving regional climate projections by driving a regional model with intermediate global simulations that use de-biased sea-surface conditions based on observations, thereby correcting for errors in the parent coupled climate model before downscaling.",
    "task": "The task is to review literature relating Antarctic climatic trends to changes in the ice sheet\u2019s surface mass balance (SMB), assessing current knowledge, model limitations, and uncertainties in future projections.",
